e in using the technology, resistance from teachers, complex technology, costly technology, and technical issues, such as connectivity problems." data-hid="citation_abstract-399300"><meta name="prism.volume" content="10" data-hid="prism.volume-399300"><meta name="prism.number" content="16" data-hid="prism.number-399300"><meta name="prism.startingPage" content="5660" data-hid="prism.startingPage-399300"><meta name="citation_firstpage" content="5660" data-hid="citation_firstpage-399300"><meta name="citation_volume" content="10" data-hid="citation_volume-399300"><meta name="citation_issue" content="16" data-hid="citation_issue-399300"><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/10/16/5660">
